This Jenkinsfile is an EFS Validation script 
Current status:
- The agent used not is mounting successfully the EFS.

Status:
- This Jenkinsfile works fine - the EFS is mounted fs was change permision to write only for test purposes.

Purpose:
- It validates the EFS mount by checking if the directory is mounted.
- It creates a file in the EFS to confirm write access.
- It prints the contents of the EFS directory to verify the file creation.
- It uses a custom Docker image with kubectl installed for Kubernetes operations.

